From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Witold=20Bo=C5=82t?= <witold.bolt@jit.team>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 06:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 9/9] egl/drm: treat a GBM back buffer without a DRI image as
 an allocation failure

gbm_dri_bo_create() falls back to create_dumb() -- a dumb buffer with
bo->image == NULL -- when the screen reports no dma-buf export (or the caller
asks for GBM_BO_USE_WRITE). get_back_bo() accepted such a buffer, so
dri2_drm_image_get_buffers() returned success with image_mask = BACK and
back = NULL, and dri2_allocate_textures() dereferenced it at the first
eglMakeCurrent.

Warn, destroy the buffer and fail get_back_bo() instead, exactly like any other
back-buffer allocation failure: getBuffers then fails, eglSwapBuffers reports
EGL_BAD_ALLOC and gbm_surface_lock_front_buffer() returns NULL, which the
client can check, instead of Mesa faulting inside eglMakeCurrent.

Defensive only: with a driver that exports dma-bufs this path is never taken.
---
 src/egl/drivers/dri2/platform_drm.c | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/egl/drivers/dri2/platform_drm.c b/src/egl/drivers/dri2/platform_drm.c
index 72e636e9f86..c52be2371a2 100644
--- a/src/egl/drivers/dri2/platform_drm.c
+++ b/src/egl/drivers/dri2/platform_drm.c
@@ -294,6 +294,18 @@ get_back_bo(struct dri2_egl_surface *dri2_surf)
             gbm_bo_create(&dri2_dpy->gbm_dri->base, surf->base.v0.width,
                           surf->base.v0.height, surf->base.v0.format, flags);
       }
+      /* gbm_dri_bo_create() falls back to a dumb buffer without a DRI image
+       * when the screen reports no dma-buf export: nothing can render into
+       * it. Treat that as an allocation failure instead of handing the
+       * frontend a NULL image.
+       */
+      if (dri2_surf->back->bo &&
+          gbm_dri_bo(dri2_surf->back->bo)->image == NULL) {
+         _eglLog(_EGL_WARNING, "DRI2: GBM surface buffer has no DRI image "
+                 "(dumb-buffer fallback: the driver reports no dma-buf export)");
+         gbm_bo_destroy(dri2_surf->back->bo);
+         dri2_surf->back->bo = NULL;
+      }
    }
    if (dri2_surf->back->bo == NULL)
       return -1;
